cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "Chunking verdicts under count- and budget-matched retrieval: code, pre-registrations and results"
abstract: >-
  Code, pre-registrations, deviation logs, run manifests and per-query results for a pre-registered multiverse
  analysis of how the retrieval-selection protocol (a fixed number of chunks vs a fixed word budget) changes
  chunking verdicts in retrieval-augmented generation, with an extension to semantic chunking and dense retrieval,
  an exploratory answer-quality check and a protocol audit of recent chunking studies.
authors:
